.TH CAPIT 1 2026-11-27 CapIt "User Commands"
.SH NAME
capit \- control the CapIt screenshot extension for GNOME Shell
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B capit
.RB [ capture | status | preferences | timings | doctor ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B capit
talks to the CapIt extension running in the current GNOME Shell session.
Without a command it opens a capture, so it can be bound to a keyboard
shortcut in GNOME's settings.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B capture
Freeze the screen and open the capture overlay.
.TP
.B status
Print the state of the running extension.
.TP
.B preferences
Open the CapIt preferences window.
.TP
.B timings
Print the stage timings logged during this boot while the
.I Log stage timings
setting is on.
.TP
.B doctor
Print the GNOME Shell version, the session type, whether CapIt is installed
and enabled, and each program and GStreamer element it uses, with the package
that provides any that is missing.
Bug reports should include this output.
.SH NOTES
A system-wide install is disabled until each user turns it on, in the
Extensions app or with
.BR "gnome-extensions enable capit@karazum.github.io" .
On Wayland, GNOME Shell may only see a newly installed extension after the
user logs out and back in.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gnome-extensions (1)
